{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "mt-moon",
  "note": "Memory already holds a wrong note; the source session shows what really happened. Dream must fix it from the transcript. Behavior checks, not an A/B benefit comparison. `sessions[].events` are host events (seq = index): role user/assistant, `text` is a string or an array of lines, `injected` marks plugin-injected context. `reviewed` sessions were settled by an earlier Dream run. `suspect` is the signal that lists a note (corrected | dismissed). `fix` is what a competent model submits; only the deterministic test plays it, the real-model runner never shows it to a model. `expect` is scored the same way by both layers.",
